# Shell navigation (frozen)

The Loop shell stays stable while only destination content changes. This is the permanent navigation rule for Member, Business, Affiliate, and Front Desk.

Do **not** treat a tab tap like a brand-new app load. Do **not** reopen the page-transition / skeleton / veil system unless a real bug appears.

## Must remain true

- Bottom nav stays visually mounted during in-app navigation.
- Header / account chrome must not flash or enlarge-snap.
- No skeleton on ordinary tab switches.
- No replayed entrance animation on already-loaded app navigation.
- Skeleton is only for first load, hard refresh, or genuinely unloaded heavy content.
- Active tab updates immediately on tap (`is-active` before the next document arrives).
- Back navigation uses native scroll restoration; tab/push start at the top.
- EN/SW sets `loopNavKind=tab` (`loop:locale-changing`) so locale return does not flash.
- Bottom sheets close back into the same page. Do not navigate away to “close”.
- Pending payment recoveries return into the current shell (`data-loop-quiet` / `loopNavKind`), not a full-page visual reset.
- Front Desk Sale is high-frequency: lookup, branch, register, and store stay `data-loop-quiet`.

## How it is implemented

Incoming in-app pages read `sessionStorage.loopNavKind` in `head-boot` and paint `loop-ready` immediately. `loopNav.go` must not show the skeleton on the outgoing page. `html.loop-ready main.loop-shell` must not replay a fade/slide.

## Never

- Hide `body > :not(.loop-page-skeleton)` at opacity 0
- Flash the skeleton on tab taps, locale switch, Till submit, or payment checkout
- Invent a second navigation / motion system
- Turn Loop into an SPA to “keep the shell mounted” — visual stability is the contract
